# /etc/logrotate.d/notetaker-remote — the remote vault audit log (specs 06/07/08).
#
# Required settings (Packages/RemoteServer AuditLog depends on them):
#   copytruncate  the service keeps its O_APPEND descriptor; truncation is seen
#                 on the next write and logging continues in the same file.
#                 (A rename+create rotation is also detected — inode check at
#                 most once a minute and whenever the size ceiling trips — but
#                 copytruncate is the supported mode.)
#   maxsize 64M   rotate early under a flood, far below the service's 256 MB
#                 ceiling, past which only forensic events (login.denied,
#                 refresh.reuse, code.reuse, kill) are written.
#   rotate 90     90 days of history (design 00 §4.8).
#   (maxsize is only evaluated when logrotate runs: spec 08 should run the
#   logrotate timer hourly, not just daily, for it to bite during a flood.)
#   su            the log directory is notetaker:adm 0750 (spec 08); logrotate
#                 refuses a non-root-writable directory without it.
# Spec 08's ct/setup.sh installs this file as /etc/logrotate.d/notetaker-remote.
/var/log/notetaker-remote/audit.jsonl {
    su notetaker adm
    daily
    copytruncate
    maxsize 64M
    rotate 90
    compress
    missingok
    notifempty
}
